{"id":"fs_138","fact":"CLI-Anything (HKUDS, 36.5k★) — protocol for making any existing GUI software agent-native by wrapping it in a CLI harness + SKILL.md. Philosophy: \"Today's Software Serves Humans. Tomorrow's Users will be Agents.\" Ships with its own CLI-Hub package manager (pip install cli-anything-hub), supports Blender, QGIS, Obsidian, n8n, FreeCAD, Godot, Inkscape, Audacity, ComfyUI, MuseScore and dozens more via community-contributed harnesses. Has CLA process, CI validation, and e2e test suite. v0.3.0+ with public registry and skill generation pipeline. Signals standardization of the 'agent skill' distribution format — parallel ecosystem to Hermes skills, OpenClaw skills, and tech-leads-club/agent-skills. Important because it represents the 'make existing tools agent-compatible' approach vs building native agent tools.","source":"https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything (GitHub Trending #3, 36,525★, May 20 2026)","date":"2026-05-20","tags":"stable,agents,cli,automation,software-architecture,interface-design,ecosystem","confidence":0.92}
{"id": "fs_139", "fact": "Agora-1 (Odyssey ML, Oliver Cameron) is a multi-agent world model that decouples simulation state from visual rendering — enabling up to 4 participants (human or AI) to share and interact within the same real-time generated world simulation. Uses GoldenEye as test environment. Architecture: one model learns gameplay state evolution from player actions, another DiT-based model renders visual from shared state. Represents paradigm shift from single-agent world models (SANA-WM) to shared simulated reality. Future roadmap: extending to foundation world models and multi-agent RL.", "source": "https://odyssey.ml/introducing-agora-1 (HN 42pts, May 19 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "stable,AI,world-model,multi-agent,simulation,gaming,research", "confidence": 0.9}
{"id": "fs_140", "fact": "Modal achieved 40x reduction in GPU inference cold starts (15s→~400ms) using: Cloud Buffers (idle GPU pool), FUSE custom filesystem (lazy container image loading), Checkpoint/Restore, and CUDA-checkpoint. Makes truly serverless GPU inference economically viable — critical infrastructure for autonomous agents that need on-demand inference without minutes of startup latency.", "source": "https://modal.com/blog/truly-serverless-gpus (HN 48pts, May 19 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "stable,AI,inference,serverless,GPU,infrastructure,agents", "confidence": 0.88}
