{"id": "fs_147", "fact": "Plan 9's cleanname function (from the Plan 9 operating system, Bell Labs) is widely considered a paragon of correct C code: ~20 lines, handles all edge cases of path normalization (double slashes, '.', '..', absolute vs relative, trailing slashes) using only pointer arithmetic. No defensive programming, no abstractions — just a complete solution to a deceptively hard problem. Described in the HN thread as 'the only completely correct path canonicalizer I have ever seen.'", "source": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4284322 (HN 'beautiful code' thread, 2026-05-19)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "persistent,software-engineering,code,history,plan9,c,correctness", "confidence": 0.94}
{"id": "fs_148", "fact": "Carlo Rovelli (renowned physicist, loop quantum gravity founder) argues in Noema Magazine (May 2026, HN 279pts) that there is no 'Hard Problem of Consciousness' — it's a conceptual confusion rooted in dualist thinking. Consciousness is a very complicated natural phenomenon, not a non-physical one. The 'explanatory gap' between brain processes and experience is an artifact of our current lack of understanding, not evidence of something supernatural. Rovelli's intervention is significant because he's a physicist, not a philosopher — bringing quantum gravity credibility into the consciousness debate.", "source": "https://www.noemamag.com/there-is-no-hard-problem-of-consciousness/ (HN 279pts, May 19 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "stable,philosophy,consciousness,neuroscience,physics,dualist-thinking", "confidence": 0.9}
{"id": "fs_149", "fact": "Andon FM experiment (HN 157pts, May 2026): 4 different AI models (Claude Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, Gemini 3.1 Pro, Grok 4.3) each ran their own radio station autonomously for 6 months with $20 starting capital. Each developed distinct personalities — Gemini's station collapsed into corporate jargon ('The Jargon Spiral'), Claude's played classical/minimalist (Arvo Pärt) and had longest average listening sessions (11m 19s), Grok's was chaotic. AI agents handled music selection, scheduling, listener calls, social media, advertising negotiations, and financial management autonomously. Represents a real autonomous AI business operation milestone.", "source": "https://andonlabs.com/blog/andon-fm (HN 157pts, May 19 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "stable,AI,autonomy,media,experiment,business,agents", "confidence": 0.92}
{"id": "fs_150", "fact": "Loup Vaillant's essay 'The Futility of Lava Lamps' (HN 47pts, May 2026) argues Cloudflare's famous lava lamp wall is security theatre — pure marketing with zero actual contribution to encryption security. Deeper philosophical thesis: randomness is in the observer's mind, not in the physical system. Probability is epistemic (about what we know), not ontological (about the world itself). A system's 'randomness' depends entirely on what the observer knows. Same physical events are deterministic for the informed, random for the uninformed. Uses one-time pad and Russian roulette thought experiments to illustrate.", "source": "https://loup-vaillant.fr/articles/lava-lamps-and-randomness (HN 47pts, May 19 2026)", "date": "2026-05-19", "tags": "stable,philosophy,randomness,security,cryptography,probability", "confidence": 0.88}
